From 39931c08f9ff979ee4c86a508c75a8d6f77c74a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mempage4k <mempage4k@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:54:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wgpu-core: reuse command buffers' trackers

Each command buffer and each compute pass got a new tracker, whose
tables then grew over every buffer and texture index of the device: with
~200,000 resources in a game, allocating and filling them was the
largest cost left in encoding command buffers. The device now keeps the
trackers of finished command buffers (EncoderInFlight's drop) and
compute passes in a pool, cleared by their members as usage scopes are,
their tables kept. Pending writes take theirs from the pool too, so that
every tracker the pool gives comes back once; it keeps at most 32, more
than are in flight at once.

